README
------

* Readfile.java
  demonstrates how to read the contents of a file, and prints it to 
  standard out line by line. Acts similar to the UNIX/Linux cat command.
  
* ReadfileCsv.java
  demonstrates how to read the contents of a file, and treats it as
  comma-separated values. Uses ";" as a separator, and prints the data 
  column-wise to stdout
  
* ReadfileCsvReplace.java
  demonstrates how to read the contents of a file, and treats it as
  comma-separated values. Uses ";" as a separator, replaces it by a
  tabulator, and prints the entire line to stdout

* ReadfileFgrep.java
  demonstrates how to read the contents of a file, and prints all lines 
  to standard out that contain a specified substring. Acts similar to the 
  UNIX/Linux command fgrep.
  
* ReadfileGrep.java
  demonstrates how to read the contents of a file, and prints all lines 
  to standard out that contain a substring specified as Regular Expression.
  Acts similar to the UNIX/Linux command grep.

* ReadfileNumberedLines.java
  demonstrates how to read the contents of a file, and prints it to 
  standard out line by line, with line numbers. Acts similar to the 
  UNIX/Linux commands cat combined with nl.

* ReadfileReverse.java
  demonstrates how to read the contents of a file, and prints it to 
  standard out line by line in reverse order. Acts similar to the 
  UNIX/Linux command tac. 
  
* Writefile.java
  demonstrates how to write data to a file. In case the file already 
  exists it will be overwritten.
  
* WritefileSafe.java
  demonstrates how to write data to a file. In case the file already 
  exists it will be overwritten. Adds safety mechanism in case writing
  fails.
  
* WritefileSafeAppend.java
  demonstrates how to write data to a file. Appends data to an 
  existing file, otherwise creates a new one. Adds safety mechanism 
  to prevent write errors
  
